</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Q1: Is a single per-frame token enough?</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We start with the most basic question: is a single per-frame token enough to support long-horizon control? We sweep the per-frame token count and report success rate, throughput, and memory.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T4.fig1" class="ltx_table ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_align_floatright" style="width:207.0pt;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Per-frame token count sweep on MetaWorld MT50 (<math id="S5.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H{=}30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H{=}30</annotation></semantics></math>). The full-token regime is infeasible at this horizon under our hardware budget; after training for 30K steps with LoRA, smaller token counts dominate.</figcaption>
