<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Sensitivity to the Fusion Softmax Temperature</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We sweep the temperature <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> used in the softmax that produces the view-level fusion weights <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> (Sec. <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Per-Frame Compression via Adaptive Attention Pooling ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ One Token Per Frame: Reconsidering Visual Bandwidth in World Models for VLA Policy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>). Tab. <a href="#A2.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Appendix B Sensitivity to the Fusion Softmax Temperature ‣ One Token Per Frame: Reconsidering Visual Bandwidth in World Models for VLA Policy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> reports the result on LIBERO. Within the range we tested, a sharper fusion (<math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau{=}0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau{=}0.1</annotation></semantics></math>) gives the highest average success in this sweep, with the largest improvement on the Long suite. We use <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau{=}0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau{=}0.1</annotation></semantics></math> in all main-paper experiments.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T10" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>Sensitivity of the fusion softmax temperature <math id="A2.T10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> on LIBERO.</figcaption>
