<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Choice of the Distance Metric in the Flow-Matching Loss</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> formulations of the velocity-field regression for the action branch and the latent branch, with all other settings held fixed (Tab. <a href="#A3.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ Appendix C Choice of the Distance Metric in the Flow-Matching Loss ‣ One Token Per Frame: Reconsidering Visual Bandwidth in World Models for VLA Policy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>). The <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}/L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}/L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> configuration is the best-performing variant in this comparison on LIBERO, with the largest gain on the Long suite. We use <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}/L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}/L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> in all main-paper experiments.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T11" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 11: </span>Sensitivity to the distance metric used in the flow-matching loss for the action and latent branches, evaluated on LIBERO (<math id="A3.T11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H{=}5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H{=}5</annotation></semantics></math> at training and inference).</figcaption>
