<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Inference-Time Configuration on LIBERO</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For LIBERO we use a single training checkpoint across all four suites and only tune the inference action horizon (AH) and the replan step on a small held-out subset of demonstrations. The exact configuration that produced the numbers in Tab. <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.1 Main Results ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ One Token Per Frame: Reconsidering Visual Bandwidth in World Models for VLA Policy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> is summarized in Tab. <a href="#A4.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ Appendix D Inference-Time Configuration on LIBERO ‣ One Token Per Frame: Reconsidering Visual Bandwidth in World Models for VLA Policy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>; the trained weights are unchanged across all reported entries. We report this protocol explicitly so that readers can reproduce the LIBERO numbers from a single checkpoint.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T12" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 12: </span>Inference-time configuration of OneWM-VLA on LIBERO. The same training checkpoint (train AH<math id="A4.T12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{=}20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{=}20</annotation></semantics></math>) is used for all four suites; only the inference action horizon (AH) and the replan step are selected per suite on a small validation grid.</figcaption>
